{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded","id":105908,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Wolf-Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-04T17:07:48-07:00","id":105908,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Wolf-Blooded","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wolf-blooded/\" target=\"_blank\">Come, your kin are waiting for you.</a><br /> <br /> What do I think of the Wolf-blooded?<br /> <br /> Hmm. This is different. 1)We're broadening the ways in which one can play a werewolf archetypally, and that's a good idea-I don't think I've seen Werewolf yet show the thousand faces of it's source beast as much as Idigam seems to be doing with both locks of extreme harmony and now the various Tells of Wolf-Blooded. 2) YES, VARIED PACKS FROM HUMANS TO WEREWOLVES AND THE BLOODED BETWEEN! I have a thing for cult/gang combos, and the involvement of the wolf-blooded and humans feels very much like that. It tickles my innards. 3)Actually, the Wolf-Blooded are a real show of the evolution of the minor template, and they really do feel like significant players in the game now, rather than simply a resource.<br /> <br /> On a different note, but still related, I've often viewed Werewolf as a game of lineages and expectations in the absence of prevalence for other things. THe Wolf-Blooded communicate this marvelously, even if they include a few ways that it's not longer tied to family lines. But that's neither here nor there really, and it's straying away from things I'd really like to look at(Er, this side tangent, not the blog).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-04-2014, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:20:16-07:00","id":105916,"title":"","content":"Stew's managed to pack in a lot of hints about stuff in this week's article <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:28:04-07:00","id":105920,"title":"","content":"It's like he wants to drive us nuts or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:30:11-07:00","id":105922,"title":"","content":"Liking it, I felt wolf-blooded always felt too much like kin.<br /> <br /> Also, no more unihar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:37:07-07:00","id":105926,"title":"","content":"EDIT: I stand corrected as a big dumb dumbo,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:51:33-07:00","id":105935,"title":"","content":"Let's see... humans actually in a pack with werewolves (not only Blooded)... who can mate among themselves... They're basically ditching <b>-Forsaken-</b> as the subtitle with this. I wanna see how they're gonna reinforce the themes of isolation from both worlds after these changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:53:19-07:00","id":105936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=105916#post105916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stew's managed to pack in a lot of hints about stuff in this week's article <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah he did. I read through the blog post and thought to myself &quot;Self, I wonder if anyone caught the almost throwaway comment of two werewolf parents?&quot; *gets down to comments* &quot;Yup, someone did. Nifty!&quot;<br /> <br /> Not that my post has anything to do with anything. Everyone just ignore me. I'll slink back into the shadows now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:59:31-07:00","id":105940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=105936#post105936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah he did. I read through the blog post and thought to myself &quot;Self, I wonder if anyone caught the almost throwaway comment of two werewolf parents?&quot; *gets down to comments* &quot;Yup, someone did. Nifty!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it kinda stood out XD<br /> <br /> Stew said that Unihar were dropped because they had unfortunate implications. I'm quite curious what those implications are,myself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:59:44-07:00","id":105941,"title":"","content":"One wonders if isolation is even a theme.<br /> <br /> I mean, it should be, it's a staple of the thematic core of werewolf mythos tied irreversibly to the theme of loss of self-control(through anger or through the horrors of biology or whatever), and the tying of the werewolf mythos to animist cultures and roles only strengthens that divide...but if I'm honest with myself, I always felt like Forsaken struggled with that theme, and I do wonder if it has evolved to a point where it's not as primary an issue as it could be-at least, it's not given more due than it would be for anyone else(save Promethean, because fuck man, how's a werewolf <i>ever</i> going to compete with them on isolation?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:03:13-07:00","id":105943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=105935#post105935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's see... humans actually in a pack with werewolves (not only Blooded)... who can mate among themselves... They're basically ditching <b>-Forsaken-</b> as the subtitle with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I don't agree. The term 'Forsaken' was never about the Uratha connection with humans. Pure have no more of an easy/hard time relating to humans than Forsaken do.<br /> <br /> Or put another way, could you please expand on your point, because I don't think A leads to B from what you've written so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:18:14-07:00","id":105953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=105935#post105935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's see... humans actually in a pack with werewolves (not only Blooded)... who can mate among themselves... They're basically ditching <b>-Forsaken-</b> as the subtitle with this. I wanna see how they're gonna reinforce the themes of isolation from both worlds after these changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite agree with this statement since I have never seen the plot as isolation and misery amongst humankind. It is a game of Savage Fury not Emo Furball. That, and from another viewpoint, this helps foster some good roleplay as Wolf-Blooded before, paired with the original descriptors of how abusive Uratha are to their families was extremely limiting. Now, they can have families that they care for rather than abuse, have mates and children who can be told of their heritage without rolling the Harmony dice who can help them with their work, and should they so choose, give them a sense of importance in otherworldly matters that are actually meaningful.<br /> <br /> Before, Wolf-Blooded were simply a minor throw in type of character who at best did nothing, and at worst, became hunters to kill you for being such an abusive parental figure.<br /> <br /> If they needed to ditch those aspects of the original book, I think it is a much healthier direction. Leave Vampires to their isolation and emo tendencies and give Werewolves the pack they deserve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:20:42-07:00","id":105954,"title":"","content":"The term Forsaken was coined by two constants: the innate hatred of the spirit world for taking up your duties against it's balance breaking freedom; and the instant divide with human society born from your spiritual side, the fact that after little stimuli you can catch yourself eyeing a human like a talking burger (or the fact that a werewolf's pragmatism with regards to human life makes a fanatic vigilante seem like a saint by comparison).<br /> <br /> Your place isn't in either world, you have to carve it tooth and claw along with the only ones who'll ever truly, spiritually understand you: your pack. Of whom, regardless of the bond, you couldn't find the required special someone there, because A) they were your spiritual siblings and that union carried with severe, severe consequences and B) to regard a single packmate, or human mate above the well-being of your pack as a whole was a step away from betrayal.<br /> <br /> The above conflicts are effectively nullified.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that, indeed, Promethean overkills you with it's isolation theme, but Forsaken's was cool, because it was something you could taste and savor, it didn't bashed you up the head with a pipe like the Created does.<br /> <br /> I just kinda wanna see if it's still gonna be enforced in some way, or we should ditch the subtitle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 04-04-2014, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:22:17-07:00","id":105956,"title":"","content":"I enjoyed the unihar, sad to see them go but I can always put 'em back in if I want. I'm sure whatever comes up should be interesting.<br /> <br /> Anyone notice this?<br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">And some embrace an entirely different Hunt \u2013 one that maintains a <i><b>Vigil</b></i> against all the monsters in the world, not just the Uratha.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:26:47-07:00","id":105958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=105956#post105956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoyed the unihar, sad to see them go but I can always put 'em back in if I want. I'm sure whatever comes up should be interesting.<br /> <br /> Anyone notice this?<br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">And some embrace an entirely different Hunt \u2013 one that maintains a <i><b>Vigil</b></i> against all the monsters in the world, not just the Uratha.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I did indeed. Looks like some crossover bait <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:31:41-07:00","id":105959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=105954#post105954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term Forsaken was coined by two constants: the innate hatred of the spirit world for taking up your duties against it's balance breaking freedom; and the instant divide with human society born from your spiritual side, the fact that after little stimuli you can catch yourself eyeing a human like a talking burger (or the fact that a werewolf's pragmatism with regards to human life makes a fanatic vigilante seem like a saint by comparison).<br /> <br /> Your place isn't in either world, you have to carve it tooth and claw along with the only ones who'll ever truly, spiritually understand you: your pack. Of whom, regardless of the bond, you couldn't find the required special someone there, because A) they were your spiritual siblings and that union carried with severe, severe consequences and B) to regard a single packmate, or human mate above the well-being of your pack as a whole was a step away from betrayal.<br /> <br /> The above conflicts are effectively nullified.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that, indeed, Promethean overkills you with it's isolation theme, but Forsaken's was cool, because it was something you could taste and savor, it didn't bashed you up the head with a pipe like the Created does.<br /> <br /> I just kinda wanna see if it's still gonna be enforced in some way, or we should ditch the subtitle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your viewpoint more clearly now, thanks.<br /> <br /> My opinion would be 'Forsaken' and isolation is still relevant; wait for Stew to provide his detail on packs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:35:25-07:00","id":105960,"title":"","content":"Maybe not?<br /> <br /> Look, let me level here with something personal. The reason I went to Werewolf first(back in my second year of high school), before any other WoD game, and why I like werewolves has always had to do with two factors.One was wish fulfillment, becuase yay I love wolfies and I'm not a strong person in life so it'd be awesome to just have this amazing strength come out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> The other was how profoundly alone I was in my youth.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of factors that tie into it, but if I had to summarize, it would be a)I had anger issues as a kid, as well as generally sharp emotions, and b) I often looked at the world very differently from my peers. on the emotional front, I just had very little sense of restraint. If i felt like I loved, I tormented myself over it, if I felt cruel, I found no limits, if I felt righteous, I acted like a tsunami, and if I felt angry, I fought. It didn't matter how little a thing was, if it made me feel something, I felt it improportionally large and acted in accordance. I fought a lot of people. None of that did me any favors. On the perspective point, I was an intellectual, I understood things a lot of my peers didn't, and everything was colored in very different ways for me. I was aware in ways they never could be, not for years to come.<br /> <br /> Sound like Werewolf? It should.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have ways to connect, and when it works it works. But there's a reason I really want to see Kuruth. For as much as it seems like the Uratha are slowly being accepted, Death Rage still remains. Those large, sharp emotions that people respond with to small things will always be one big reason they'll always be Forsaken.<br /> <br /> When it easier for people to get closer, it's also easier to hurt them. Even if you don't want to.<br /> <br /> PS: Oh, and just because I'm a jerk-Hey,Dessembrae?<br /> <br /> I won again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-04-2014, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:37:19-07:00","id":105961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=105954#post105954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term Forsaken was coined by two constants: the innate hatred of the spirit world for taking up your duties against it's balance breaking freedom; and the instant divide with human society born from your spiritual side, the fact that after little stimuli you can catch yourself eyeing a human like a talking burger (or the fact that a werewolf's pragmatism with regards to human life makes a fanatic vigilante seem like a saint by comparison).<br /> <br /> Your place isn't in either world, you have to carve it tooth and claw along with the only ones who'll ever truly, spiritually understand you: your pack. Of whom, regardless of the bond, you couldn't find the required special someone there, because A) they were your spiritual siblings and that union carried with severe, severe consequences and B) to regard a single packmate, or human mate above the well-being of your pack as a whole was a step away from betrayal.<br /> <br /> The above conflicts are effectively nullified.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that, indeed, Promethean overkills you with it's isolation theme, but Forsaken's was cool, because it was something you could taste and savor, it didn't bashed you up the head with a pipe like the Created does.<br /> <br /> I just kinda wanna see if it's still gonna be enforced in some way, or we should ditch the subtitle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must gently disagree. Not to say that you're wrong, certainly there are elements of isolation that appear to be leaving the system (Physical passion and abusive parenthood). However, while those elements would certainly be sources of isolation in real life, they did not reflect that in play. I mean, how often does a characters inability to have carnal relations with another Werewolf affect play? And when was the last time you had a scene in which a PC Werewolf lost his cool and beat his child?<br /> <br /> Idigam, from what I can tell, retains the most relevant source of isolation, the chance that you could transform into a massive killer wolf-monster and maul all those around you. And adds a few new ones via Harmony: Getting too close to the man, and being unable to effectively run with your pack. Or getting too close to the spirit and being literally locked out of the material. Those are forms of isolation the player will <b>feel.</b> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:59:58-07:00","id":105969,"title":"","content":"I think in Idigam Chronicles, they are focusing much more on just what it means to be a feral creature, and how being close to one can affect you. Think about it, just by being near you, your perfectly human sister or mother can become a Dalu taking monster. A chance encounter with one can have the same effect. Just by existing, you can ruin lives and put people in danger without intending to.<br /> <br /> But then again, you are also a wolf, and wolves have packs. Your wolf-blooded and your fellow uratha are the closest to you. You may want to avoid hurting anyone by breeding with other werewolves, or you might risk it by looking for a human mate. It is no longer about anger, it is about making them into monsters like you.<br /> <br /> But you cannot be solely a werewolf, either, because doing that will make you too spirit. But succesfully hiding among humans means you might one day explode and kill who you love, and leave wolf-blooded going after you blood.<br /> <br /> So it is a tightrope walk, constantly being pushed to be more spirit or more human. And you belong to neither world fully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T19:03:07-07:00","id":105973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=105961#post105961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idigam, from what I can tell, retains the most relevant source of isolation, the chance that you could transform into a massive killer wolf-monster and maul all those around you. And adds a few new ones via Harmony: Getting too close to the man, and being unable to effectively run with your pack. Or getting too close to the spirit and being literally locked out of the material. Those are forms of isolation the player will <b>feel.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>And the nature of Tells seems to be building on the concept that I really liked <b>The Rage</b>'s phrasing of:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Rage, pg202, sidebar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[C]ertain themes are universal across the board when it comes to the Forsaken. <b>Werewolves are born of violence, exile and suffering.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T19:21:25-07:00","id":105982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=105961#post105961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must gently disagree. Not to say that you're wrong, certainly there are elements of isolation that appear to be leaving the system (Physical passion and abusive parenthood). However, while those elements would certainly be sources of isolation in real life, they did not reflect that in play.<b> I mean, how often does a characters inability to have carnal relations with another Werewolf affect play? And when was the last time you had a scene in which a PC Werewolf lost his cool and beat his child?</b><br /> <br /> Idigam, from what I can tell, retains the most relevant source of isolation, the chance that you could transform into a massive killer wolf-monster and maul all those around you. And adds a few new ones via Harmony: Getting too close to the man, and being unable to effectively run with your pack. Or getting too close to the spirit and being literally locked out of the material. Those are forms of isolation the player will <b>feel.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>As often as I wanted? I mean, right, it's not for every table, and I'm not going to give you a statistic, but yes, it came around often. Particularly in the department when you have a packmate side with another one over an objective issue, and the guilt they may feel for putting someone above the whole in a certain aspect. I'm not saying it has to go back to what it was. I'm saying I wanna see what's gonna be written to make Werewolves feel Forsaken with all their pack buddies and &quot;perfectly capable of defending themselves&quot; spouses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T19:25:38-07:00","id":105986,"title":"","content":"Side speculation: Is there gonna be a <b>Ritual</b> to cement a Tell into the auspices of a true spiritual heritage and mark a Wolfblooded as one of the Uratha? Seems most likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T22:34:59-07:00","id":106054,"title":"","content":"Things I like: <br /> \u2022 Wolf-Bloods don\u2019t necessarily mean \u201cmommy or daddy was a werewolf\u201d. Both might have been, or neither. I\u2019m willing to bet that Skin-thieves are now another way to become wolf-blooded. <br /> \u2022 Ghost Children are gone, as is the taboo against Uratha mating with Uratha. <br /> \u2022 Wolf-Blooded feel a lot like werewolves in and of themselves \u2014 actual werewolves, not human/spirit hybrids who can turn into wolves. They can shapeshift!<br /> <br /> Interesting note: as of 38 comments, there have been 26 votes: 13 for Auspices and 13 for Packs. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T22:37:46-07:00","id":106056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106054#post106054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things I like:<br /> \u2022 Wolf-Bloods don\u2019t necessarily mean \u201cmommy or daddy was a werewolf\u201d. Both might have been, or neither. I\u2019m willing to bet that Skin-thieves are now another way to become wolf-blooded.<br /> \u2022 Ghost Children are gone, as is the taboo against Uratha mating with Uratha.<br /> \u2022 Wolf-Blooded feel a lot like werewolves in and of themselves \u2014 actual werewolves, not human/spirit hybrids who can turn into wolves. They can shapeshift!<br /> <br /> Interesting note: as of 38 comments, there have been 26 votes: 13 for Auspices and 13 for Packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's awesome. I love these close votes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Wolf-blooded are now the minor template Forsaken needed AND the one it deserved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-05-2014, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T23:55:57-07:00","id":106081,"title":"","content":"No way I'm going to ditch the Unihar.<br /> <br /> I always liked to present the Unihar and their creation as a little similar to Rose's thoughts on the embrace - they're a very little understood fact of werewolf nature, and you're tempting fate by having hot wolf-on-wolf action. She might or might not get pregnant, and the child might or might not be wolf-blooded. The lower your Harmony, the more prone you are to death rage, the higher the probability that your own kid will be a creature that exists only to kill wolves.<br /> <br /> I also enjoyed the implications of the result of two werewolves mating being a true monster. Shouldn't the child of two werewolves be a creature that's, like, more werewolf-y than werewolves? Makes you think about the nature of werewolves.<br /> <br /> I like the new wolf-blooded!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T00:00:50-07:00","id":106082,"title":"","content":"If werewolves can breed with their own kind than there's nothing forcing a connection to humanity against their nature, Uratha can now form their own completely separate societies and avoid close human contact without risking the survival of their species. It's an IMMENSE amount of dramatic tension let out of the game!<br /> <br /> Even if the Unihar are problematic, werewolves can still be infertile with their own kind and thus the survival of the species still requires human mating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T00:07:48-07:00","id":106083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106082#post106082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If werewolves can breed with their own kind than there's nothing forcing a connection to humanity against their nature, Uratha can now form their own completely separate societies and avoid close human contact without risking the survival of their species. It's an IMMENSE amount of dramatic tension let out of the game!<br /> <br /> Even if the Unihar are problematic, werewolves can still be infertile with their own kind and thus the survival of the species still requires human mating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because sex is the only reason anyone could ever have to connect with someone, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T00:21:32-07:00","id":106091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106083#post106083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because sex is the only reason anyone could ever have to connect with someone, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well unless you're a sadist who gets off on power and torture, you're generally not going to seek those connections with someone whose instinctively terrified of you who you run a substantial risk of flipping out and murdering - not when there's an entire community of beings like you with whom that isn't a problem you can form those connections with.<br /> <br /> Hence the removal of the REQUIREMENT for human connection to preserve the species removing an entire central horror element of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-05-2014, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T00:29:23-07:00","id":106095,"title":"","content":"I do hope that the unihar remain in some capacity to fill the role of somewhat-implacable-agent-of-a-werewolf's-demise, if only because it feels like a compelling antagonist space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T00:40:53-07:00","id":106101,"title":"","content":"Man, I was hoping they could make the Wolf-Blooded as interesting a choice as B&amp;S ghouls, and they sure have delivered! I'm going to be curious to see how Packs work.<br /> <br /> (If Sleepwalkers/Proximi work out as well in Fallen World Chronicles and half-Demon children are cool, I am so going to do a Minor Splat Chronicle)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T00:55:51-07:00","id":106114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106082#post106082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If werewolves can breed with their own kind than there's nothing forcing a connection to humanity against their nature, Uratha can now form their own completely separate societies and avoid close human contact without risking the survival of their species. It's an IMMENSE amount of dramatic tension let out of the game!<br /> <br /> Even if the Unihar are problematic, werewolves can still be infertile with their own kind and thus the survival of the species still requires human mating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see this more as &quot;when two werewolves mate they, in some rare instance, <b>can</b> create Unihar&quot;. So werewolves can fell love with they kind, only it's a bit dengerous, - most of the time they produce more werewolves and wolf-blooded, but from time to time... Think more about parents having kids after 40's, there is just so much more percent of it having genetic and mental disorders,<br /> <br /> It leaves a part of horror parenthood without forcibly banning it. Makes humans and wolf-blooded more suitable mates. Also, sustain and even inforce the suspance - &quot;we don't know if your children want be murderous spirits hunting our kind - Werewolf soon-to-be dad: I will take a chance!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-05-2014, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T01:37:47-07:00","id":106142,"title":"","content":"@Unihar:<br /> <br /> Even if werewolves can now successfully mate with each other they will not always produce offspring that will actually (or even can) experience the First Change and Werewolves are not that numerous to begin with and their numbers are constantly dwindling through violent death. Therefore many Werewolves will still have to breed with humans and wolf-blooded as a simple fact of MATHEMATICS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T02:06:43-07:00","id":106152,"title":"","content":"@Unihar: What about a really Spirit harmony-attuned Werewolf gives birth to something more spirit and less &quot;flesh&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T02:11:30-07:00","id":106158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106082#post106082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If werewolves can breed with their own kind than there's nothing forcing a connection to humanity against their nature, Uratha can now form their own completely separate societies and avoid close human contact without risking the survival of their species. It's an IMMENSE amount of dramatic tension let out of the game!<br /> <br /> Even if the Unihar are problematic, werewolves can still be infertile with their own kind and thus the survival of the species still requires human mating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you could introduce a sliding scale of likelihood of undergoing First Change, ranging from Uratha-Uratha = very, very low chance (most likely wolf-blooded), Uratha-Wolf-Blood = some chance, Uratha-human = greatest chance.<br /> <br /> In this way, if the Uratha don't want to die out in a generation or two, they need to cleave to the humans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T02:29:02-07:00","id":106163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106152#post106152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Unihar: What about a really Spirit harmony-attuned Werewolf gives birth to something more spirit and less &amp;quot;flesh&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> That would make sense to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T03:11:11-07:00","id":106174,"title":"","content":"Am I the only person who is amused that we've got posts worrying about both how werewolves will now be able to have families and relationships with humans and wolf-blooded more easily now, and how they'll be able to retreat away from humanity into their own societies more easily now, both within a short distance of each other? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I don't mean this as a dig at the posters in question, just that the internet is an amazing thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Remember that, as ever, Stew's weekly design posts only shine light on a small portion of the game and don't give you all the context of how it interacts with the rest. Declarations that Uratha are no longer Forsaken or that they no longer need humanity may be premature!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T04:35:34-07:00","id":106207,"title":"","content":"As I stated in the blog, I have actual experience over games where uratha can breed with one another. And you'd be surprised how -little- it actually changed the game, people still wanted to play wolf-blood and uratha still claimed wolfbloods.<br /> <br /> Also, it is good to remember that the new harmony is about balance. You can't have that balance if you never go around humans. So even if you could breed with other uratha, there are still plenty of reasons not to avoid humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T08:21:40-07:00","id":106279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106207#post106207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I stated in the blog, I have actual experience over games where uratha can breed with one another. And you'd be surprised how -little- it actually changed the game, people still wanted to play wolf-blood and uratha still claimed wolfbloods.<br /> <br /> Also, it is good to remember that the new harmony is about balance. You can't have that balance if you never go around humans. So even if you could breed with other uratha, there are still plenty of reasons not to avoid humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, I could imagine not interacting with humans regularly could be a Breaking Point towards Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T09:00:26-07:00","id":106309,"title":"","content":"On the Unihar, I'm actually part of the minority that liked them, but unlike some of the others, I'm not worried about their removal for a couple of reasons. They've been a major complaint for the majority of the fanbase for a while, and with good reason, and the implementation of a more pack-based mentality in werewolves is a good idea. What's more is that we're only getting small glimpses and Stew mentioned something like them might come in later, so it's not like things are solidly set.<br /> <br /> And that's last part is the big thing about these blogs-we don't know. I think it's better to just wait and see if these subjects come up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:06:46-07:00","id":106355,"title":"","content":"Looking ahead to packs: If they're going with a more wolves-in-the-real-world structure (as I think the MIGHT) I wonder if you might have older, more experienced parent Wolf-Blooded be more in charge of a pack than full Uratha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:28:41-07:00","id":106404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106355#post106355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking ahead to packs: If they're going with a more wolves-in-the-real-world structure (as I think the MIGHT) I wonder if you might have older, more experienced parent Wolf-Blooded be more in charge of a pack than full Uratha?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Totem is okay with it, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:39:54-07:00","id":106413,"title":"","content":"I do wonder if packs might actually be familial by default now that such a thing is possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T12:26:41-07:00","id":106443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106413#post106413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder if packs might actually be familial by default now that such a thing is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would certainly help with the issue of buy-in that I've always had with <i>Werewolf.</i><br /> <br /> Between the increasing presence of the 'monster inside trying to tear its way out' angle (which never really existed in <i>Forsaken</i> and was always handled better by Vampire) and the decreasing problems with buy-in (I've never really been able to answer the question of &quot;why does a newly Changed werewolf bother doing the spirit-cop thing, and is there anything else that this game can do?&quot;), <i>Idigam Chronicles</i> might well get me back on board the Werewolf bandwagon. This is really exciting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1812-deflare","name":"Deflare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T12:33:53-07:00","id":106447,"title":"","content":"*Silently facepalms and refuses to feed the troll*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T13:09:46-07:00","id":106470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106447#post106447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Silently facepalms and refuses to feed the troll*</div> </div> </div> </div>...which troll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T13:30:22-07:00","id":106482,"title":"","content":"If you're referring to Deflare, he's not trolling. That's actually a very common sentiment among people who want to like Forsaken, but have never been able to get into it. One that I share. Forsaken as presented in the core just doesn't resonate with most peoples' perceptions of werewolves. The game is cool once you get into it, but that initial buy in is a big obstacle for a lot of people. Especially because the focus is primarily on the external threats from the Shadow and the Pure, where the &quot;traditional&quot; (relad: most prevalent in pop culture) Werewolf story is much more focused on the internal threat of the wolfman's own nature. It is seeming like the Direction Idigam is moving in is one that starts closer to that Wolfman story and eases you into the spirit cop game, so people have an easier time bridging that initial gap of &quot;why should I care about all this spirit crap?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:12:45-07:00","id":106503,"title":"","content":"Because the spirits, the hosts, and all that spirit crap is going to care about you, regardless of your stance on it. But since I don't ST your table...<br /> <br /> I would just introduce an Azlu who eats the brain of you character's best friend and then transforms him into it's husk to properly eat you, because ignorant, rebellious Ghost Wolves are tasty, and easy prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:23:37-07:00","id":106516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106503#post106503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the spirits, the hosts, and all that spirit crap is going to care about you, regardless of your stance on it. But since I don't ST your table...<br /> <br /> I would just introduce an Azlu who eats the brain of you character's best friend and then transforms him into it's husk to properly eat you, because ignorant, rebellious Ghost Wolves are tasty, and easy prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they were talking more about a player stance, rather than a character stance - the game has, presumably, too much focus on Spirits for their taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:43:00-07:00","id":106533,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Hey guys, please don't accuse other users of trolling, if you feel someone is trolling then use the Flag function and let the mods handle it. Thanks.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:18:33-07:00","id":106555,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the spirit game, I think its a very cool take on Werewolves. But it's a definite departure from their depiction in most pop culture, which makes it difficult to hook new players into. What it needs (and what it seems like Idigam is doing) is giving new players a more recognizable (dare I say archetypal?) werewolf to dip their toes in with, and a positive incentive to join a pack and protect a territory. Because honestly, if I were to kill off a new player's character's friends and family, their reaction is not going to be &quot;gee, I'd better start paying attention to this spirit stuff.&quot; It's going to be &quot;this game sucks, lets just go back to Vampire&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:11:51-07:00","id":106591,"title":"","content":"By the sound of this preview, I think I'm going to enjoy the Wolf-Blooded more than I like the full-blown Uratha.<br /> <br /> ...and now I find myself wanting to play a Wolf-Blooded game that has a heavy focus on Spirits and a handful of Ulgan Prometheans as antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:17:32-07:00","id":106597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106591#post106591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the sound of this preview, I think I'm going to enjoy the Wolf-Blooded more than I like the full-blown Uratha.<br /> <br /> ...and now I find myself wanting to play a Wolf-Blooded game that has a heavy focus on Spirits and a handful of Ulgan Prometheans as antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, I think there could be a lot of mileage in using the minor splats (Wolf-Blooded, Ghouls and their Families, Sleepwalkers/Proximi) as the basis of a crossover Chronicle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:19:04-07:00","id":106598,"title":"","content":"I am now personally waiting for the inevitable game where I play a Wolf-Blooded toddler who then has a conversation go as follows<br /> <br /> Toddler: &quot;Daddy? What is the strange glowing thing in the closet that looks like a floating head?&quot;<br /> Dad: &quot;Don't worry about it son, it's just a minor spirit of fright. Would you like me to maul it for you?&quot;<br /> Toddler: *nods*<br /> Dad: SUPER WEREWOLF MODE ACTIVATE!!!<br /> Toddler: &quot;Thanks dad! Your the best!&quot;<br /> <br /> Then there were hugs all around and much rejoicing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 04-05-2014, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:20:21-07:00","id":106600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106597#post106597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Seriously, I think there could be a lot of mileage in using the minor splats (Wolf-Blooded, Ghouls and their Families, Sleepwalkers/Proximi) as the basis of a crossover Chronicle</div> </div> </div> </div> That could be a lot of fun. I love that minor splats are finally getting to be cool in their own right, instead of just being [primary splat] lite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:24:22-07:00","id":106603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106600#post106600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That could be a lot of fun. I love that minor splats are finally getting to be cool in their own right, instead of just being [primary splat] lite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and it means there's not as much in the way of the background cruft and noise while still holding their primary splat's flavour. Come on, a game dealing with the politics that arise when a Wolf-Blooded, Proximi and Ghoul families go at each other's throat, with half-Demons acting as free agents? That's a damn fine urban fantasy story right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:31:29-07:00","id":106609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106598#post106598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am now personally waiting for the inevitable game where I play a Wolf-Blooded toddler who then has a conversation go as follows<br /> <br /> Toddler: &quot;Daddy? What is the strange glowing thing in the closet that looks like a floating head?&quot;<br /> Dad: &quot;Don't worry about it son, it's just a minor spirit of fright. Would you like me to maul it for you?&quot;<br /> Toddler: *nods*<br /> Dad: SUPER WEREWOLF MODE ACTIVATE!!!<br /> Toddler: &quot;Thanks dad! Your the best!&quot;<br /> <br /> Then there were hugs all around and much rejoicing</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcy likes. Arcy wants. Arcy will use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T18:29:04-07:00","id":106648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106555#post106555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind the spirit game, I think its a very cool take on Werewolves. But it's a definite departure from their depiction in most pop culture, which makes it difficult to hook new players into. What it needs (and what it seems like Idigam is doing) is giving new players a more recognizable (dare I say archetypal?) werewolf to dip their toes in with, and a positive incentive to join a pack and protect a territory. Because honestly, if I were to kill off a new player's character's friends and family, their reaction is not going to be &quot;gee, I'd better start paying attention to this spirit stuff.&quot; It's going to be &quot;this game sucks, lets just go back to Vampire&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The Shadow is my favorite of the WoD 'alternate realms', and spirits are really cool. I also like werewolves as the monster within thrashing to get out. The problem <i>Forsaken</i> held to me was getting from the monster within (which basically isn't a problem after your First Change, since Kuruth is hard to trigger at decent Harmony if you don't wade into a fight often) to the cool spirit stuff in a way that didn't feel forced or constricting. I also just had a basic problem with the idea that a <i>Forsaken</i> chronicle consists of staking out your territory, and then stopping whatever monster of the week the GM through at you; it's a solid game premise, but rather limiting to be the main premise in chronicle after chronicle.<br /> <br /> The new version looks like it's really diversifying the story of the Forsaken and the people linked to them, taking parts of the original version that fell a bit flat and giving them new life and flare. This is all for the better, regardless of whether or not you had qualms with <i>Forsaken</i>'s premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1812-deflare","name":"Deflare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T19:28:58-07:00","id":106666,"title":"","content":"Upon reflection, I\u2019ve come up with some further observations and questions:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Now that Wolf-Blooded is a lesser template, I presume that it\u2019s no longer a Merit. In effect, the Wolf-Blooded are like <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Proximi and <b>Changeling</b>\u2019s Fae-Touched. Kudos! But will <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> include anything like \u201cSleepwalker\u201d or \u201cEnchanted Mortal\u201d? That is, a Merit that doesn\u2019t grant any supernatural powers other than resistance or immunity to whatever passive, ambient, mind-warping effect the greater template in question gives off (that is, Lunacy)? <br /> <br /> \u2022 Do the Wolf-Blooded have Primal-Urge 0, the way <b>Blood and Smoke</b>\u2019s ghouls have Blood Potency 0? <br /> <br /> \u2022 Are there any Tells that derive from the spiritual side of the Uratha\u2019s nature, the way the one that grants regeneration draws from the physical side? <br /> <br /> \u2022 Do the Wolf-Blooded have access to any supernatural powers other than their Tell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T19:52:37-07:00","id":106675,"title":"","content":"What I got out of it is that since now anyone can become Wolf-Blooded, and since there's a portion of Wolf-Blooded that can become Uratha, Humanity has an equal chance of becoming a Werewolf as they would have a Mage. Food for thought there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T20:29:52-07:00","id":106686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106666#post106666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upon reflection, I\u2019ve come up with some further observations and questions:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Now that Wolf-Blooded is a lesser template, I presume that it\u2019s no longer a Merit. In effect, the Wolf-Blooded are like <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Proximi and <b>Changeling</b>\u2019s Fae-Touched. Kudos! But will <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> include anything like \u201cSleepwalker\u201d or \u201cEnchanted Mortal\u201d? That is, a Merit that doesn\u2019t grant any supernatural powers other than resistance or immunity to whatever passive, ambient, mind-warping effect the greater template in question gives off (that is, Lunacy)?<br /> <br /> \u2022 Do the Wolf-Blooded have Primal-Urge 0, the way <b>Blood and Smoke</b>\u2019s ghouls have Blood Potency 0?<br /> <br /> \u2022 Are there any Tells that derive from the spiritual side of the Uratha\u2019s nature, the way the one that grants regeneration draws from the physical side?<br /> <br /> \u2022 Do the Wolf-Blooded have access to any supernatural powers other than their Tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you not read the examples of Wolf-Blooded acting as Loci, acting as speakers for spirits, and having Reaching in regards to the gauntlet?<br /> <br /> Spiritual side is definitely a-showing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T21:30:48-07:00","id":106714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106591#post106591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the sound of this preview, I think I'm going to enjoy the Wolf-Blooded more than I like the full-blown Uratha.<br /> <br /> ...and now I find myself wanting to play a Wolf-Blooded game that has a heavy focus on Spirits and a handful of Ulgan Prometheans as antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026I'm reminded of how reading the Wolf-Blooded chapter of Blood of the Wolf made me want to run a wolf-blooded Scooby Doo game where Scooby is the only werewolf in the gang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T23:42:46-07:00","id":106755,"title":"","content":"Man, the voting is really, really close, by my estimation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T01:09:00-07:00","id":106779,"title":"","content":"Wolf-Blooded could always become Uratha, nothing prevented it. You might be mixing it up with WtA's Kinfolk there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T02:53:09-07:00","id":106803,"title":"","content":"I wonder how different this conversation about &quot;the monster within&quot; part of Forsaken would be if Kuruth had got chosen instead...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T02:57:09-07:00","id":106804,"title":"","content":"A wolf-blooded who's subject to kuruth and turns Dalu under the full moon is pretty much your lon chaney / jack nicholson werewolf right there. No need for the full template, just like minor hege magicians are better done as Sleepwalkers than fully Awakened mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T03:08:55-07:00","id":106806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Charlaquin</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106413#post106413\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I do wonder if packs might actually be familial by default now that such a thing is possible.</span><br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> </span><br /> That would certainly help with the issue of buy-in that I've always had with <i>Werewolf.</i><br /> <br /> Between the increasing presence of the 'monster inside trying to tear its way out' angle (which never really existed in <i>Forsaken</i> and was always handled better by Vampire) and the decreasing problems with buy-in (I've never really been able to answer the question of &quot;why does a newly Changed werewolf bother doing the spirit-cop thing, and is there anything else that this game can do?&quot;), <i>Idigam Chronicles</i> might well get me back on board the Werewolf bandwagon. This is really exciting to me.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>I think you would like to read Skinchangers. Personally, I find the Skin-Thieves minor template more accurate to the traditional werewolf than the Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T04:25:24-07:00","id":106823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106804#post106804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A wolf-blooded who's subject to kuruth and turns Dalu under the full moon is pretty much your lon chaney / jack nicholson werewolf right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I now want to run Wolf-Blooded miniChronicle that prepering them for being Uratha as Jack Nicholson movie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106804#post106804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need for the full template, just like minor hege magicians are better done as Sleepwalkers than fully Awakened mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it a spoiler for <b>Fallen World Chronicle</b>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T09:14:04-07:00","id":106930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106823#post106823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it a spoiler for <b>Fallen World Chronicle</b>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely hope that the Proximii get a boost of weirdness that would make them as fun to play as the Wolf-Blooded and the Ghouls.<br /> Currently, I'm find Second Sight Thaumaturges far more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mumm