","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T09:39:28-07:00","id":106941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106940#post106940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Votes are pretty damn tight now 35 Packs/28 Auspices</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm expecting Packs to win mostly because of all the hints that were dropped about it in this latest blog. Which is fine by me. I voted for Auspice because after Harmony that was the next big thing I wanted to hear more about, but I'm as curious as everyone about how Mortals and Wolf Blooded are going to be integrated into packs of Uratha. My guess is still that they're familial now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T09:44:09-07:00","id":106943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105908-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-wolf-blooded?p=106941#post106941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm expecting Packs to win mostly because of all the hints that were dropped about it in this latest blog. Which is fine by me. I voted for Auspice because after Harmony that was the next big thing I wanted to hear more about, but I'm as curious as everyone about how Mortals and Wolf Blooded are going to be integrated into packs of Uratha. My guess is still that they're familial now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't surprise me if they were, or (less likely) merit based - a person has to prove themselves to a Totem to join a pack, it's just easier for an Uratha to do so than any one.<br /> <br /> Hmmmm... I wonder if a human joining a Pack makes them immune to the Lunacy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T12:12:19-07:00","id":107017,"title":"","content":"Personally, if Auspice don't win, I hope they're at least in the next vote, because freaking Wolfbloods had been in two votes on a row.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/